---
description: >-
  Label syntax (#1368, #1400): the ishikawa effect, causes and sub-causes at two depths, each
  kind written as plain markdown markers, a quoted markdown string, bare backticks, a code span
  in plain text, tags and a written `\n`. Only a line that is wholly a quoted markdown string is
  markdown; bare backticks and plain markers are drawn as written; tags draw and `\n` breaks.
  There is one effect, so it shows the markdown string only.
---
ishikawa-beta
  "`effect **bold** _ital_`"
  cause **bold** _ital_
    sub **bold** _ital_
  "`cause **bold** _ital_`"
    "`sub **bold** _ital_`"
      "`deep **bold** _ital_`"
  `cause **bold** _ital_`
    `sub **bold** _ital_`
  cause a `code` b
    sub a `code` b
  cause <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O
    sub <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O
  cause one\ntwo
    sub one\ntwo
